  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 1001.05 Eligibility for Surface Water Treatment Supplemental Grants.\n\n(a) In order to be eligible for surface water treatment supplemental grants in the amount of 10% of the total eligible surface water treatment costs, the water system shall:\n\n(1) Demonstrate to the department that construction will result in user fees for the average single family home that are 20% above the statewide average for residential customers as established by the department pursuant to Env-Dw 1001.06; and\n\n(2) Meet all eligibility requirements of Env-Dw 1001.03.\n\n(b) The effect of the 10% supplemental grant shall not be included in the amount used to calculate eligibility under this section.\n\n(c) Where a system uses the fixture rate method, a list of all customers and their charges for the previous year shall be submitted to the department.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Ws 300) #6521, eff 6-4-97; ss by #8360, INTERIM, eff 6-4-05; ss by #8479, eff 11-30-05 (see Revision Note at part heading for Env-Dw 1001) (formerly Env-Ws 393.05); ss by #10616, eff 6-1-14; ss by #14121, eff 11-23-24, EXPIRES: 11-23-34",
